## Reviewed exceptions

These are not blanket-allowed by the policy and carry obligations beyond
attribution, so they are named here rather than left to a generated list. The
reasoning for each is recorded in the policy document's "Reviewed exceptions"
table and must stay in agreement with it.

| Package        | Licence   | Obligation ARQ accepts                                                                                                                                            |
| -------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `web-ifc`      | MPL-2.0   | Consumed as a compiled library through its published API and never forked or patched in-tree. MPL-2.0's copyleft covers modifications to its own source files; ARQ makes none. If ARQ ever patches it, the patched files must be published under MPL-2.0. |
| `caniuse-lite` | CC-BY-4.0 | Browser-compatibility data reached as a build-time transitive dependency, not linked into the product bundle. Attribution is carried by this entry and by the generated bill of materials. |

Do not assume the ARQ repository licence covers model weights, datasets, fonts,
icons, or downloaded sample files — check each of those independently.
